    "proof": "Moves use distinct initially-empty new cells and separate vehicles. Every subset is legal, all cube edges are physically replayed. Any pair needs at least one slide per changed vehicle; cube paths attain that Hamming count, hence these distances are exact in the FULL physical graph. Each different antipodal pair requires a separate active absolute-difference coordinate: two length-k pairs on one coordinate imply cross-distance sum>=2k, but their true cross sum<=2k-2. Thus exact Linf embedding of all2^k cube vertices needs at least2^(k-1) coordinates. A shared coordinate forces worst absolute distance error>=0.5. Normalized L1 represents this independent subgraph additively.",
